  "key_findings": [
    "Throughput scales with NODES, not cores. Doubling nodes at a fixed slot count roughly halved per-task time; doubling slots on fixed nodes bought about 1.10x.",
    "Per-task median is a function of tasks-per-node: ~13.5s at 8/node, ~21s at 16/node, ~37s at 32/node.",
    "The cost driver reverses by dataset: corr(n_train, time) was +0.52 on reddit and -0.02 on products, while corr(n_edges, time) was -0.01 on reddit and +0.62 on products. No single balancing heuristic is correct for both.",
    "reddit cannot demonstrate scalability at any cluster size: usable parallelism is 36 under every partitioner tested (louvain, leiden, lpa, igraph_lpa all give 22-24 on member counts).",
    "Phase 3 carries a serial floor of roughly 40-55s (load, broadcast, collect) that never parallelises."
